  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>From the figure<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/7121bbc6-feb3-4d01-935a-86fb5b0ee0f2.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 230px; height: 167px;\" /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math><br /><math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, angle subtended by the statue at the eyes of the observer is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac></math></p>",
